. Did bootstrap create it, or skip it?

kubectl -n amp-ra logs deploy/ldapportal-backend | grep -i bootstrap
Bootstrap: created LOCAL superadmin [superadmin] → the account was made with the secret's password → your problem is likely a value mismatch or wrong username (below).
Bootstrap skipped — N active LOCAL superadmin(s) already exist → the secret password is being ignored; the real password is whatever the first boot used.
2. What password does the running pod actually hold, and is it what you typed?

kubectl -n amp-ra exec deploy/ldapportal-backend -- \
  printenv BOOTSTRAP_SUPERADMIN_USERNAME BOOTSTRAP_SUPERADMIN_PASSWORD
Check for: a trailing newline (classic from echo instead of printf when creating the secret), YAML quoting eating a special char, or that you edited the Secret but never restarted the backend (envFrom only reads at pod start — editing a Secret does not roll the pods).

Also: log in with the username superadmin (the BOOTSTRAP_SUPERADMIN_USERNAME from configmap.yaml), not an email.

Fix
If it says "created" but login still fails → the stored password is exactly what's in that printenv output (trailing whitespace and all). Set the secret cleanly and re-bootstrap:

kubectl -n amp-ra create secret generic ldapportal-secrets \
  --from-literal=BOOTSTRAP_SUPERADMIN_PASSWORD='YourPassword' \
  ... (other keys) --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
(use single quotes; avoid echo).

If it says "skipped" → the env var can't help until the existing superadmin is gone. For a dev deploy with no real data, drop it and let bootstrap recreate it with the current secret:

# make sure the Secret has the password you want FIRST, then:
kubectl -n amp-ra exec ldapportal-db-0 -- psql -U ldapportal -d ldapportal -c \
  "DELETE FROM superadmin_permission_grants; \
   DELETE FROM accounts WHERE role='SUPERADMIN' AND auth_type='LOCAL';"

kubectl -n amp-ra rollout restart deploy/ldapportal-backend
kubectl -n amp-ra logs -f deploy/ldapportal-backend | grep -i bootstrap   # expect "created"
That clears the account (and its permission grant, which has an FK to it), so existingCount is 0 on the next boot and bootstrap re-creates superadmin with your current password and owner permissions.

Run the two diagnostic commands and tell me which log line you get — that pins whether it's "inert secret" (reset path) or "value mismatch" (clean-secret path). My strong bet, given all the DB recreation: "Bootstrap skipped."

kubectl -n amp-ra port-forward deploy/ldapportal-backend 8080:8080 &
curl -i -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"username":"superadmin","password":"YOUR_PASSWORD"}'

kubectl -n amp-ra exec ldapportal-db-0 -- psql -U ldapportal -d ldapportal -c \
  "DELETE FROM superadmin_permission_grants; DELETE FROM accounts WHERE role='SUPERADMIN' AND auth_type='LOCAL';"
kubectl -n amp-ra rollout restart deploy/ldapportal-backend

